<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-internship-regulatory-affairs-all-genders-berlin-268814> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-20T10:35:46+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/sunday-natural/internship-regulatory-affairs-all-genders-berlin-268814> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "fa48d627f430a0a844737072487d0ad426aee82ed525dc6ca2f842e283307ed6" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-19T18:41:05+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-20T10:35:46+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "internship-regulatory-affairs-all-genders-berlin-268814" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-19"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Berlin | Full-time, 40 hours per week | 6 months | Start: October Your role We are looking for a motivated Intern for our Regulatory Affairs Team to support our experienced team with the regulatory review of our products and a wide range of research projects. During your internship, you will gain practical insights into regulatory affairs within the food supplement industry and contribute to both the team’s daily business and new product launches. You will work across different topics, support the entire Regulatory Affairs team and use modern tools, including AI, to conduct and structure research. If you identify with our products and our vision and would like to develop your regulatory knowledge in a hands-on environment, we would be happy to welcome you to our team. You conduct regulatory and scientific research on ingredients, product claims, labelling requirements and relevant legal developments. You support the team with day-to-day operational tasks related to new products, product changes and portfolio reviews. You use AI and other digital tools to research, structure and summarise regulatory information efficiently. You help prepare documentation and internal overviews for regulatory projects. Depending on your experience and development, you take ownership of defined research topics and smaller projects. Depending on your language skills in other languages of our countries of sales, you support in country-specific regulatory topics Your profile You are currently enrolled in a university programme in Food Chemistry, Nutritional Sciences, Nutrition and Home Economics, Food Technology or a comparable field of study. You are available for a full-time internship of six months and remain enrolled throughout the internship. You have an interest in EU food law, food supplements and regulatory affairs. Initial academic or practical knowledge in these areas is an advantage. You enjoy conducting detailed research and are curious about using AI tools to support your work. You work carefully, reliably and in a structured manner. You are proactive, hands-on and comfortable supporting the team across a broad range of topics. You are confident using Google Workspace or comparable digital tools. You have German and English language skills at B2 level or above. You are based in Berlin or willing to relocate to Berlin for the duration of the internship. What we offer An appealing discount on all of our products – from essential oils to vitamins & nutrients Ownership and plenty of room for new initiatives, with the opportunity to contribute your expertise and turn your own ideas into action Hands-on experience in a dynamic environment and insight into the regulatory environment of a fast growing consumer brand Opportunities to contribute to real projects and make an impact Inviting office spaces with access to plenty of organic teas and superfoods from around the world in which we meet 3-4 days per week Sunday Natural emerged from a long-standing passion and research in the fields of health, healing, and personal growth. The lack of natural, high-quality products on the market was the original motivation for founding Sunday Natural in 2013. We aim to produce the products we ourselves would love to buy – as natural as possible, absolutely pure, free from any additives, and of the highest quality. In a strategic partnership with CVC, Sunday Natural is now one of Germany's most renowned quality manufacturers, with its own research and development department in Berlin. For the continuous improvement of our products, we collaborate with selected research institutes, scientists, therapists, farmers, and professional associations. We take our ecological responsibility very seriously: that’s why the majority of our product range is vegan. We also take an innovative approach to packaging: most of our products are packaged in glass, making them almost entirely recyclable. Our diverse team in Berlin consists of over 400 employees from more than 45 nationalities and continues to grow – but at a sustainable pace. Our goal is to foster a collaborative, supportive, and inclusive work environment with a diverse group of motivated, talented, and visionary team members. We highly value equality of opportunity and inclusivity, and we would like to particularly encourage women and candidates from under-represented backgrounds to apply, even if you don’t match with 100% of the requirements. Legal Notice Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
