    schema:description "Applied Intuition, Inc. is powering the future of physical AI. Founded in 2017 and now valued at $15 billion, the Silicon Valley company is creating the digital infrastructure needed to bring intelligence to every moving machine on the planet. Applied Intuition services the automotive, defense, trucking, construction, mining and agriculture industries in three core areas: tools and infrastructure, operating systems, and autonomy. Eighteen of the top 20 global automakers, as well as the United States military and its allies, trust the company’s solutions to deliver physical intelligence. Applied Intuition is headquartered in Sunnyvale, California, with offices in Washington, D.C.; San Diego; Ft. Walton Beach, Florida; Ann Arbor, Michigan; London; Stuttgart; Munich; Stockholm; Bangalore; Seoul; and Tokyo. Learn more at applied.co. We are an in-office company, and our expectation is that full-time employees primarily work from their Applied Intuition office 5 days a week. However, we also recognize the importance of flexibility and trust our employees to manage their schedules responsibly. This may include occasional remote work, starting the day with morning meetings from home before heading to the office, or leaving earlier when needed to accommodate family commitments. This in-office expectation does not apply to contractor positions Senior Fullstack Engineer UK Full-time /London (Engineering) About Applied Intuition Defence Applied Intuition UK is a software and infrastructure supplier that accelerates the deployment of next-generation autonomous capabilities to the warfighter across air, land, sea, and space. A subsidiary of Applied Intuition, we deliver dual-use solutions to national security customers that build upon several years of product development and experience from commercial autonomy programs. Based in London, our seasoned defence team hails from Palantir, Anduril, SpaceX, Google, Lockheed Martin, and the UK and US Armed Services. Learn more at appliedintuitiondefense.com. About the role You would be the first fullstack engineer we hire onto the UK team, joining software and autonomy engineers whose tools are already relied on across live programmes. As that portfolio grows, we are bringing in dedicated fullstack expertise to shape how the user-facing products we ship are designed and built. Every day is different: designing an interface around how a customer actually operates, building the services and APIs behind it, working with our design team so what we ship in London is coherent with everything else Applied Intuition builds, or taking what we learn on a programme and landing it in the products of the teams we work alongside. You will move between languages and layers as the problem demands, and you will have a strong voice in how these products get built. You bring the judgement of a career spent shipping production software, and you watch the people you built it for take it into the field. At Applied Intuition, you will: Take new products from concept through to production at the pace our programmes demand, owning the technical and product decisions along the way Build features end to end, from the interface through the API to the services and data behind it Set the front-end foundations for our UK products: shared components, sensible patterns, and a design language consistent with the rest of the company Decide, with the team, when a new capability should stand alone and when it belongs in our core product offering Get the improvements we identify on programmes into the products our other teams build, so what we learn in the field shapes the wider roadmap Engineer security in from the first commit, and build software that holds up to the environments and the scrutiny our customers operate under Help raise the bar for how user-facing software is built here, and build products people depend on and that you are proud of We’re looking for someone who has: Bachelor's degree in computer science/related engineering field 5+ years of hands-on fullstack experience shipping and supporting production web applications Deep expertise in React and TypeScript, or another modern front-end framework, and strong, well-founded opinions about building interfaces for data-heavy workflows Adaptability across languages and comfort owning the whole stack; our products span TypeScript, Go and Python, and we care more about your judgement than your syntax Experience working closely with designers and product managers, and a track record of getting your requirements into products you don't own Command of application security, and experience developing in Docker and containerised environments on Linux Travel Requirements: General willingness to travel for company business between our offices, as well as to customer sites Security Requirements: Must have ability to hold UK Security Clearance (current or previous preferred) Nice to have: 7+ years of experience building fullstack applications, including time as the senior voice on front-end architecture Hands-on experience with 3D or geospatial visualisation in the browser, such as CesiumJS, Three.js or WebGL Experience building or extending a design system used across more than one team Experience deploying and operating what you build, on Kubernetes or similar Experience with autonomy, robotics, simulation or other systems that generate data at a scale browsers were never designed for Experience working on projects related to national security for one or more government agencies References who will describe them as low-ego, historically motivated, thoughtfully opinionated, strong communicators and curious listeners Don’t meet every single requirement? If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles. Applied Intuition is an equal opportunity employer and federal contractor or subcontractor. Consequently, the parties agree that, as applicable, they will abide by the requirements of 41 CFR 60-1.4(a), 41 CFR 60-300.5(a) and 41 CFR 60-741.5(a) and that these laws are incorporated herein by reference. These regulations prohibit discrimination against qualified individuals based on their status as protected veterans or individuals with disabilities, and prohibit discrimination against all individuals based on their race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or national origin. These regulations require that covered prime contractors and subcontractors take affirmative action to employ and advance in employment individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status or disability. The parties also agree that, as applicable, they will abide by the requirements of Executive Order 13496 (29 CFR Part 471, Appendix A to Subpart A), relating to the notice of employee rights under federal labor laws. FOR US-BASED ROLES: Applied Intuition is committed to providing an accessible and inclusive application and interview experience to applicants who are disabled veterans and other applicants with disabilities or medical conditions. Reasonable accommodations are available, requesting an accommodation will not affect your candidacy in any way, and you are not required to disclose the nature of your disability or medical condition in order to make a request. If you require an accommodation please contact Compensation: $100K – $160K • Offers Equity • $100K – $160K • Offers Equity Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
