    schema:description "TL;DR — alago brings AI-powered project management to the construction industry. As our Product Manager, you'll own a core product area end to end: how messy project data becomes an early warning that a €200M project is about to go wrong. Full-time, Munich. About alago Imagine if building a building were as easy as building software. Every moving part visible, every change traceable, every decision still carrying its reasoning six months later. Software got there by making its own history legible — every commit, every diff. Construction never did. A €200M project runs on plan sets nobody can diff and decisions buried in email, so the same mistakes happen over and over, and the industry loses $1.6 trillion a year to it. That's what we're fixing. Eleven people, 15+ customers, €1M+ pre-seed from leading construction-tech VCs and one of Germany's largest project developers. The product is live and used daily on real construction sites — which means the interesting work is only starting. Tasks What you'll do Translate deeply technical construction workflows into decisions engineers can build from Own a product area end to end: From discovery on site to shipped, instrumented, measured features Shape the roadmap: Balance what the next customer needs against the foundations that make the next ten cheap Make the hard prioritization calls on scope and sequencing, and defend them Define what \"working\" means: pick the metrics, instrument them, read production data, iterate Treat LLM behavior as a product problem, not a research one — evals, fallbacks, and what the user sees when the model is wrong Requirements Must-haves 2+ years shipping product — as a product manager, or as a UI/product designer who's been making product calls and not just screens You've shipped something where the hard part was the data model, not the button Hands-on experience with LLM-powered features in production — you know what breaks and how users react when it does Genuine willingness to put on boots and go on site until you know the domain better than we do Bonus AEC background Founder experience, or product work at a company under 20 people You already build your own agents and internal tools to do your job faster Not a match on every line? Apply anyway — potential and learning curve count. Benefits You'll be one of our first product hires, which means you own critical parts of the product end to end and work directly with the founders. It's early enough that you help decide how the company works, and the path from here goes to either top individual contributor or leading product as we grow, depending on where you're strongest. Competitive compensation with equity. Hybrid: three days a week in our central Munich office (WERK1). Plus: Wellpass, team dinners twice a week, relocation support. About the application process 1. Submit your story Tell us about something you built that had real impact. 2. Intro Call (25min) Intro, Logistics & Fit with a founder. 3. Product Challenge (45min) Tackle a product challenge in person 4. Offer We’ll get back to you within 24 hours. If it’s a fit — let’s go! 🎉 Alago is an equal opportunities employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, religion, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability or gender identity. Please do not submit personal data revealing racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs, trade union membership, data concerning your health, or data concerning your sexual orientation. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
