<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-senior-sales-development-representative-bilingual-french-english-london-596> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-20T10:35:46+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/faire/senior-sales-development-representative-bilingual-french-english-london-596> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "550b7807be73924e097902cb2cc3168fdcf9d2e44d1bfc67ee0dd51b35f75e0a" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-20T01:27:27+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-20T10:35:46+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "senior-sales-development-representative-bilingual-french-english-london-596" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-19"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "<div class=\"content-intro\"><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>About Faire</strong></span></p> <p>Faire is a technology wholesale platform built on the belief that the future is local. Independent retailers around the globe collectively represent a multi-hundred-billion-dollar wholesale market that has historically been fragmented and offline. At Faire, we're using the power of tech, data, and machine learning to connect this thriving community of entrepreneurs across the globe. Picture your favorite boutique in town — we help them discover the best products from around the world to sell in their stores. With the right tools and insights, we believe that we can level the playing field so businesses can grow and local communities can thrive.</p> <p>We’re looking for smart, resourceful and passionate people to join us as we power the shop local movement. If you believe in community, come join ours.</p></div><p><strong>About this role</strong></p> <p>Faire’s quality, depth, and breadth of supply is one of our strongest value propositions to retailers, and our Enterprise Brand Partnerships team plays a critical role in bringing strategic, high-value brands onto the platform. As a Senior SDR, you will directly contribute to Faire’s growth by helping scale our enterprise supply strategy and building relationships with brands that will shape the future of our marketplace.We are looking for a strategic and highly motivated sales professional who can independently manage complex outbound prospecting motions, identify high-potential partnership opportunities, and help drive pipeline growth for our Enterprise Account Executive team. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in fast-paced environments, enjoys solving problems creatively, and is excited to contribute beyond their individual pipeline through collaboration, mentorship, and process improvement initiatives.Faire’s goal is to become the default platform for brands to grow their wholesale business and for retailers to discover products for their stores. As we continue to scale, there will be significant opportunities for ownership, impact, and career growth.</p> <p><strong>What you’ll do&nbsp;</strong></p> <ul> <li>Build and execute strategic outbound prospecting motions to engage high-value and enterprise-level brands</li> <li>Prospect, identify, and prioritize brands that are a strong fit for Faire’s retailer ecosystem and long-term marketplace strategy</li> <li>Drive qualified pipeline generation through a mix of cold calls, warm outreach, email campaigns, social selling, and creative prospecting strategies</li> <li>Customize outreach and discovery conversations based on brand pain points, category dynamics, and business goals</li> <li>Partner closely with Enterprise Account Executives to strategically manage territories, prioritize opportunities, and improve conversion outcomes</li> <li>Leverage Salesforce, reporting tools, and sales engagement platforms to track pipeline health, monitor pacing to goals, and optimize outreach strategy</li> <li>Identify workflow inefficiencies, contribute ideas for process improvement, and support broader team initiatives</li> <li>Act as a collaborative partner and trusted resource across the SDR and AE organization by sharing best practices, insights, and learnings</li> <li>Have opportunities to grow into more strategic sales, leadership, enablement, or cross-functional roles within the company</li> </ul> <p><strong>Qualifications</strong></p> <p><strong>Must Haves</strong></p> <ul> <li>A Bachelor’s degree or equivalent professional working experience</li> <li>Fluent in French and English</li> <li>Exceptionally strong verbal and written communication skills with the ability to confidently lead prospect conversations&nbsp;</li> <li>Strong organization and prioritization skills with the ability to manage a large book of prospective accounts</li> <li>Ability to tailor outreach strategies and messaging based on customer pain points and market context</li> <li>Strong business acumen and curiosity around retail, ecommerce, and marketplace dynamics</li> <li>Experience leveraging data, dashboards, and reporting tools to inform outreach strategy and identify opportunities or gaps</li> <li>Motivated, curious, action-oriented, and proactive in fast-moving environments with evolving priorities</li> <li>Passionate about Faire’s mission and helping entrepreneurs and brands grow their businesses</li> <li>Collaborative mindset with a willingness to contribute to team growth, mentorship, and process improvement</li> </ul> <p><strong>Nice to Haves</strong></p> <ul> <li>1-2 years+ of retail or customer-facing work experience</li> <li>Experience with Salesforce, Salesloft, Looker, or similar sales/reporting platforms</li> <li>Enterprise or strategic account prospecting experience</li> <li>Strong cold calling and objection handling experience</li> <li>Experience working in SaaS, marketplace, ecommerce, or startup environments</li> <li>Retail, merchandising, wholesale, or small business experience</li> <li>Entrepreneurial mindset and desire to help shape a growing sales organization</li> </ul> <p><strong>Salary Range</strong></p> <p>London, UK: the OTE pay range for this role is £56,000 to £77,000 per year.&nbsp;</p> <p>This role will also be eligible for equity and benefits. Actual base pay will be determined based on permissible factors such as transferable skills, work experience, market demands, and primary work location. The base pay range provided is subject to change and may be modified in the future.</p><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em data-stringify-type=\"italic\">Hybrid Faire employees currently go into the office 3 days per week on Tuesdays, Thursdays, and a third flex day of their choosing (Monday, Wednesday, or Friday).</em> Additionally, hybrid in-office roles will have the flexibility to work remotely up to 4 weeks per year. Specific Workplace and Information Technology positions may require onsite attendance 5 days per week as will be indicated in the job posting.&nbsp;<br></span></em></p> <p><strong>Why you’ll love working at Faire</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Move fast:</strong> You'll own meaningful problems that serve customers around the globe with the agency to move fast and see your results clearly.</li> <li><strong>Equipped to scale:</strong> We invest in what matters, including the latest enterprise AI tools, to help you work smarter and get more out of every day.</li> <li><strong>Best in class:</strong> Our team is full of sharp, kind, and generous colleagues who care about their craft and about helping you grow in yours.</li> <li><strong>Real rewards.</strong> Competitive pay, equity, and comprehensive benefits designed to support your life inside and outside of work.</li> <li><strong>Belonging:</strong> We're intentional about building an environment where every Faire employee has equal access to opportunities, growth, and success.</li> </ul> <p>Faire was founded in 2017 by a team of early product and engineering leads from Square. We’re backed by some of the top investors in retail and tech including: Y Combinator, Lightspeed Venture Partners, Forerunner Ventures, Khosla Ventures, Sequoia Capital, Founders Fund, and DST Global. We have headquarters in San Francisco and Kitchener-Waterloo, and a global employee presence across offices in Toronto, London, and New York. To learn more about Faire and our customers, you can read more on our <a href=\"https://blog.faire.com/\">blog</a>.</p> <p></p> <p>Faire provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetics, sexual orientation, gender identity or gender expression.</p> <p>Faire is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. Accommodations are available throughout the recruitment process and applicants with a disability may request to be accommodated throughout the recruitment process. We will work with all applicants to accommodate their individual accessibility needs.&nbsp; To request reasonable accommodation, please fill out our <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSczpI9me7nYKhunSC6AlagHKv75LHqfi-Qi2TP_3dpin0Uc9Q/viewform\">Accommodation Request Form</a> (<a href=\"https://bit.ly/faire-form)\">https://bit.ly/faire-form)</a></p> <p><strong data-stringify-type=\"bold\">Privacy</strong></p> <p>For information about the type of personal data Faire collects from applicants, as well as your choices regarding the data collected about you, please visit Faire’s <a class=\"c-link\" href=\"https://www.faire.com/privacy\" target=\"_blank\" data-stringify-link=\"https://www.faire.com/privacy\" data-sk=\"tooltip_parent\">Privacy Notice (https://www.faire.com/privacy)</a></p></div> Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-faire ;
